# connector: amqp_source — consume a RabbitMQ queue onto the bus (ADR-0026).
# A first-class standalone binary (connectors/amqp), pure Rust, sync, no
# tokio, no OpenSSL: TLS is rustls over amiquip's mio loop. At-least-once:
# basic.consume with manual ack — a message is acked to RabbitMQ only after
# the JetStream pub-ack, so a crash in between redelivers (no loss).
# Subjects in: (none) · out: vx.amqp.orders.in · secrets: the URL carries
# the credentials — take it from your deployment's secret machinery, never
# a literal in this file.
# Build once: cargo build --release --manifest-path connectors/amqp/Cargo.toml
# Run under your process supervisor.

AMQP_URL_NOTE="amqp:// for plaintext, amqps:// for TLS (rustls, no C)"
VEJAS_AMQP_URL="${AMQP_URL:?take amqp(s)://user:password@host:port from your secret store}"
VEJAS_AMQP_MODE=source
VEJAS_AMQP_QUEUE=orders
VEJAS_AMQP_SUBJECT=vx.amqp.orders.in
NATS_URL=127.0.0.1:4222

# TLS (amqps://): pin your CA and the server name rustls verifies against
#VEJAS_AMQP_TLS_CA=/etc/vejas/rabbitmq-ca.pem
#VEJAS_AMQP_TLS_SERVER_NAME=rabbitmq.internal

# Singleton by default BECAUSE order (ADR-0020/0026): instances contend on a
# JetStream KV lease. Opt into competing consumers — RabbitMQ delivery is
# per-message acked, so competing is duplicate-safe — when throughput
# outranks global order:
#VEJAS_AMQP_COMPETING=1
